From d88c507267fa95c43561511c35e515a8f88d7ca6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:28:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Defer remote-index reader misses to a live, beating
 holder

Card J t_01a1d862f6e2fc9e. In P1 run11, a Desktop serve's notification pollers rebuilt the whole remote
index on ~23 of 202 kanban polls. That cost 5.65 s of the poller's 8.97 s, ~1.03% of a core on its own,
which is over the 0.7% serve watcher+poller row. Cause: a poll that lands between a replica commit and the
holder's 1 s republish misses the published copy and runs compute (_index + observe) itself. The gateway
showed ~78 such misses per hour.

Five whys:
1. Why is the row over budget? poll_kanban CPU is dominated by remote_index.compute.
2. Why so many computes? Readers run them, not the holder.
3. Why do readers compute? A miss computes immediately, even when a live holder is about to publish,
   because the reader had no notion of the holder.
4. Also: a miss was memoized per stamp, so the copy the holder then published for that same stamp was
   never read until the next commit.
Why it was not caught: the existing component benches measured signatures only, never the poller with a
moving replica.

Fix (reader side only; the holder, publish format and keys are untouched): for the host's own replica and
root-home ledger, on a miss that has a change key, if a live holder of lease kanban-remote-index beat
within 5 s, the poll returns no remote cards (nothing is read, claimed or written).
- Bound: DEFER_MAX_S = 4 s from a chat's first deferred miss. That is under one 5 s poll, so a deadline
  poll never defers twice. After the bound, that chat's misses compute until a hit, so a holder that beats
  but never publishes cannot halve delivery.
- Any doubt computes at once, as before: no lease, released, dead or stale, a future-dated heartbeat, an
  unreadable lease dir, a profile home, explicit paths, or no key.
- Misses are no longer memoized.

Independent design review: APPROVE. Its two findings (an expired slot deferring again, a future-dated
heartbeat) are fixed in this commit.
Proof: test_kanban_remote_index_defer.py has 14 passing tests. RED on the base was 10 failed, on the set
before the review fixes. The consumer suite on the pre-review cut: 42 files, 594 passing.
